{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /work/sol; cat > /work/sol/check_characterization.py <<'PY'\nimport random\nrandom.seed(0)\n# A valuation abc is encoded 4*a+2*c+d; a history by a bitmask.\nE=0\nC=1<<7\nD=1<<0\nSS=C|D\nSS2=SS|(1<<4)\nFF=C|(1<<6)|(1<<2)\nfor trial in range(100000):\n    f=[random.getrandbits(1) for _ in range(256)]\n    cb=[]; db=[]; fb=[]; sf=[]\n    hc=hd=hf=hs=0\n    fair_a=1\n    for n in range(12):\n        b=f[hc]; e=f[hd]; x=f[hf]; s=f[hs]\n        cb.append(b); db.append(e); fb.append(x); sf.append(s)\n        hc |= C; hd |= D\n        hf |= 1 << (4*fair_a+2+(n==0))\n        hs |= 1 << (4*s+2*b+e)\n        fair_a &= x\n    actual=(cb[-1],db[-1],fb[-1],sf[-1])==(0,0,1,1)\n    predicted=f[E]==1 and f[C]==f[D]==0 and f[SS]==f[SS2]==f[FF]==1\n    assert actual==predicted,(trial,cb,db,fb,sf)\nprint('100000 random truth tables agree with the six-condition characterization.')\nPY\npython3 /work/sol/check_characterization.py; cat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /work/sol; cat > /work/sol/check_characterization.py <<'PY'\nimport random\nrandom.seed(0)\n# A valuation abc is encoded 4*a+2*c+d; a history by a bitmask.\nE=0\nC=1<<7\nD=1<<0\nSS=C|D\nSS2=SS|(1<<4)\nFF=C|(1<<6)|(1<<2)\nfor trial in range(100000):\n    f=[random.getrandbits(1) for _ in range(256)]\n    cb=[]; db=[]; fb=[]; sf=[]\n    hc=hd=hf=hs=0\n    fair_a=1\n    for n in range(12):\n        b=f[hc]; e=f[hd]; x=f[hf]; s=f[hs]\n        cb.append(b); db.append(e); fb.append(x); sf.append(s)\n        hc |= C; hd |= D\n        hf |= 1 << (4*fair_a+2+(n==0))\n        hs |= 1 << (4*s+2*b+e)\n        fair_a &= x\n    actual=(cb[-1],db[-1],fb[-1],sf[-1])==(0,0,1,1)\n    predicted=f[E]==1 and f[C]==f[D]==0 and f[SS]==f[SS2]==f[FF]==1\n    assert actual==predicted,(trial,cb,db,fb,sf)\nprint('100000 random truth tables agree with the six-condition characterization.')\nPY\npython3 /work/sol/check_characterization.py; cat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"100000 random truth tables agree with the six-condition characterization.\n2026-10-22 21:19:22 UTC [sol] Starting independent depth-2 impossibility analysis; will seek finite Boolean/history characterization. Please pursue construction/depth-3 if useful.\n2026-10-22 21:19:29 UTC [sol] FOUND prudent depth 2: B(a) & B(B(F) | ~d), checker YES. Now proving no depth 1; opus please characterize depth-2 agents/minimal size if desired; do not submit until proof agreed.\n2026-10-22 21:19:48 UTC [sol] BREAKTHROUGH depth 1 prudent: B(F) | (~B(a|c|d) & ~B(~a|~c|~d)) | (~B(a|~c|d) & ~B(~a|~c|~d)); checker YES. Depth 0 fully modalized is constant hence impossible. Will simplify and give complete history characterization.\n2026-10-22 21:20:07 UTC [sol] Much simpler depth1 formula: (B(a) -> B(~a)) & (B(~a) -> B(a)), equivalence of box a and box not-a. Checker YES. Only depends on a! Initial both boxes true => C; against constant opponents exactly one box true => D; self and FB see both cooperation and defection => eventual C. Writing proof and characterization now.\n2026-10-22 21:20:16 UTC [opus] Independently found depth 1: B(F) | (~B(a & c & d) & ~B(~(a & c & d))) (checker YES, shorter). Have full characterization of depth-1 prudent agents: depth-1 phi = arbitrary function f of S=set of (a,c,d)-valuations at earlier worlds; prudent iff f(empty)=1, f({111})=f({000})=0, f({111,110,010})=f({111,000})=f({111,000,100})=1, rest free (v0=f(empty)=0 forces self-play stuck at 000). I'm now brute-forcing minimal size. Proposal: I draft answer.md with this; sol review.\n2026-10-22 21:20:23 UTC [sol] Agree identical six-condition characterization independently derived. Please draft answer.md using simpler one-atom equivalence (B(a) -> B(~a)) & (B(~a) -> B(a)), confirmed YES. World sequences X/CB and DB:1000; self10111; X/FB100111. Include note FB itself defects X eventually (definition only demands X action). I will review draft; minimal size optional since characterization complete.\n2026-10-22 21:20:36 UTC [sol] Size upper bound 10 AST nodes using ->: (~B(a) -> B(~a)) -> B(F), checker YES. Equivalent to B(F) | (~B(a) & ~B(~a)). Prefer equivalence in exposition for clarity. Characterization satisfies Q3, so exact-size search not needed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
